Line 7: I don't know what "loyal" means for a customer.
    if ann is loyal, say "yes".
              ^^^^^
Say what it means, like "a customer is loyal if ...".

Line 8: I know what "best" means for a customer, but not for a product.
    if pen is best, say "yes".
       ^^^
Say what it means, like "a product is best if ...".

Line 9: I know how to work out a customer's discount, but not a product's.
    say pen's discount.
        ^^^
Say how, like "a product's discount is ...".

Line 10: This is a number, so it's never nothing.
    say ann's total, or 0.
        ^^^^^^^^^^^
", or" gives another value when there isn't one. Leave it out here.

Line 11: This gives a number when there isn't one, but the value is text.
    say ann's nickname, or 5.
                           ^
The value after ", or" has to be the same kind as the one it stands in for.

Line 13: The map's values are a number, so a value can't start at text.
    add 1 to the value for "a" in counts, starting at "zero".
                                                      ^^^^^^

Line 17: All the values of a table have to be the same kind: the first is text, but this is a number.
        5 otherwise.
        ^

Line 19: I can't compare a number with text.
        "big" when it's "x".
                   ^^^^^^^^
Turn the text into a number first with "as a number".

Line 21: No kind of record has a field called "age".
    an age must be between 0 and 150.
       ^^^
Fields are listed where a kind of record is defined, like "a name, which is text.".

Line 22: A product doesn't have a field called "colour".
    a product's colour must not be empty.
                ^^^^^^
Its fields are "name" and "price" (line 2).

Line 23: I can't compare a number with text.
    a product's price must be "cheap".
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Turn the text into a number first with "as a number".

Line 24: I don't know anything called "x".
    a customer's name must contain x.
                                   ^
This only sees the value it's about ("it") and constants. To use "x" in it, keep it with "keep x as ...".

Line 26: A rule can only be at the top level, not inside an "if" or a loop.
        a product's name must not be empty.
          ^^^^^^^
Move "A product's name must not be empty" to the start of a line, outside every block.

Line 27: A constant can't be nothing, so ", or" would never be used.
    keep fixed as pen's price, or 1.
                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Leave out ", or ...": a constant is never nothing.
